-Trace-based SDF Rendering is a technique that traces rays through a sparse voxel model using Signed Distance Fields (SDF) to determine hit depth and voxel ID, then retrieves color from the hit voxel's spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients. It differs from standard volume rendering by relying on the geometric precision of the SDF for ray marching rather than volumetric integration, and from pure mesh rendering by storing appearance data within the voxel structure rather than on triangle faces.
